        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/FF-header-7-reso.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>We already knew that <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/final-fantasy-vii\">Final Fantasy 7</a> Revelation was going to launch <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/final-fantasy-y-revelation-gamescom-new-look\">sometime in 'spring 2027</a>', but today director Naoki Hamaguchi took to Sony's State of Play livestream to inform us all that the game has a locked-in release date: 8th April, 2027. It'll launch worldwide, and on all platforms - that's PS5, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/platforms/switch-2\">Nintendo Switch 2</a>, Xbox Series X/S, and PC - at the same time (the first game in the series to do so).</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/final-fantasy-7-revelation-release-date-resonance-demo\">Read more</a></p>",
